 "result": "Use `@pass_script_info`, defined in `src/tessel/cli.py:375`. It injects the `LaunchInfo` object, and you call `info.load_app()` inside the command to get the app.\n\n- **Decorator:** `@pass_script_info` (`src/tessel/cli.py:375`), used by `run_command` at `src/tessel/cli.py:933`.\n- **Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). Its `load_app()` method (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`) resolves the app from `--app`, `TESSEL_APP`, or `wsgi.py`/`app.py`, and caches it.\n- **Registration:** the root group is `cli = TesselGroup(...)` at `src/tessel/cli.py:1109`. Attach your command with `@cli.command(...)` or `@click.command(...)` plus `cli.add_command(...)`, following the existing `shell` and `routes` commands (`src/tessel/cli.py:998`, `1047`).\n\nExample:\n\n```python\n@click.command(\"my-cmd\")\n@pass_script_info\ndef my_cmd(info: LaunchInfo):\n    app = info.load_app()\n```",
